# Review of the optimization walkthrough

Review date: 2026-10-03. This is a separate editorial and evidence audit; it does not change the walkthrough or any executable source. Root reports that v28 is built, its public cached-window policy is active, 306 focused tests pass along with memcheck, and 15 selected captured/mutating cases pass racecheck with zero errors. The full suite is still running. Whole-model paired timing and fresh native results remain pending. This review independently reads v24/v27 artifacts; it does not independently re-execute those v28 checks.

Reviewed walkthrough SHA-256: `be85e9641b81222f81acebbbe5db05fbae0365f8c778413b9fa062d24946f6ba`.

The walkthrough is candid about the remaining performance gap. Sections 25 and 26 correctly separate numerical validation, resident component timing, native physical-layout timing, and NCU measurements. The main work is to refresh the opening status, distinguish repeated observations from distinct contracts, and explain how the v27 winners enter the public dispatcher without overstating their coverage.

