## Independent checks performed for this review

Read-only JSON enumeration confirms 16 C256 reports with 96 observations / 48 distinct contracts and 16 smaller-width reports with 192 observations / 96 distinct contracts. Recomputed C256 gains are 1.246373–1.426897× against the fastest canonical/public/pair route and 1.037466–1.120415× against every other measured peer. The generated policy has 72 rows and version `86bfe65380016080`.

The v24 native audit confirms all 931 committed geometries, zero unmeasured or unsupported cases, 931 `speed_gap` statuses, and the unchanged canonical record digest `1a8a2f72b1aee583244445ae097a0b84781b9b7e47279644eac0baeed95e2ed5`. The C256 NCU report confirms 48.555954% tensor, 39.749160% L2 and 4.826854% DRAM elapsed-cycle throughput. Source inspection confirms canonical cache views and alias restoration in `InferenceBlock._apply`.

No benchmark, GPU kernel, compiler, or active-source modification was run for this audit.
